## Task

Decompose the approved design into between 1 and 3 implementation
tasks. Each task carries an `id`, a short `title`, and a list of
`acceptance_criteria` bullets.

Acceptance criteria MUST reference skill-driven build/test verbs
when installed skills teach them. Fall back to the raw commands
only when no matching skill exists.

The `tasks` array MUST always contain exactly 3 entries
(`id=t1..t3`). Fill the first `num_tasks` entries with real tasks; on
unused trailing slots set `title` to the empty string (`--set-json`)
and `acceptance_criteria` to the empty list. Unused slots run as no-ops (the slot agent emits empty outputs for an
empty title); the contract requires explicit empty values, never
omission:

```bash
$LOOM output add "{{ input.__loom.workdir }}" --task tasks-author \
    --set 'tasks[].id=t3' --set-json 'tasks[-1].title=""' \
    --set-json 'tasks[-1].acceptance_criteria=[]'
```

Set `num_tasks` to the real-task count.

## Output

```bash
LOOM=~/.kiro/skills/home/loomv2/scripts/loom.sh
$LOOM output init "{{ input.__loom.workdir }}" --task tasks-author
$LOOM output add  "{{ input.__loom.workdir }}" --task tasks-author \
    --set 'tasks[].id=t1' \
    --set 'tasks[-1].title=<title>' \
    --set 'tasks[-1].acceptance_criteria[]=<criterion>' \
    --set num_tasks=1
```
